@*
    REQ-UI-035 / REQ-UI-036 / REQ-UI-037 / REQ-UI-038 — Misses & rework, the sixth report page.

    Everything on this page comes out of the engine's MissAnalysis. The page renders it; it never
    recomputes a guarded figure by hand. The period filter narrows the *record set* and then re-runs
    MissFigures.Compute over it, so every guard — the `why_missed` denominator, the `linked`-only
    attribution, the MinN floor, the MissCost split — is applied by the same code that computes the
    unfiltered view, rather than by a second copy of the rules living in a Razor file (REQ-NFR-013).

    Five things on this page are deliberate and are not stylistic:

      1. Measured and apportioned rework cost are two columns and a count. `MissCost` exposes Sole,
         Apportioned and NoneCount and nothing else, so no control here can bind a blend (ADR-019).
      2. Every per-phase / per-model / per-agent figure is computed from MissAttributionTaint.Partition,
         and the count it held out is printed on the page (`miss-taint-count`). An exclusion the reader
         cannot see is indistinguishable from a bug (BRD-121).
      3. The failed-practice distribution prints `n of N assessed` on its face, over records that CARRY
         the field, never over the miss count (BRD-119).
      4. `wont-fix` is its own tile and never enters the open count; `deferred` always does (BRD-120).
      5. Rate-card dollars are on their own dashed card, on their own row, carrying
         RateCard.EstimateLabel and the `_usd_estimate` export key. Nobody was billed that amount
         (BRD-123).
*@
@page "/misses"
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Text.Json
@using System.Text.Json.Nodes
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using TfLens.Core.Metrics
@* These namespaces are NOT in Components/_Imports.razor and Razor does not fail the build when a
   component cannot be resolved — it emits RZ10012 and renders the tag as an unknown element with no
   styling. Same fix as Routing.razor. *@
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.Empty
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.Typography
@using TfLens.Components.Shared.Playbook
@using TfLens.Components.Pages.ExportParts
@implements IDisposable
@inject ITelemetryStore objStore
@inject IOptions<TfLensOptions> objOptions
@inject ShellPreferences objPreferences

<PageTitle>Misses &amp; rework · TfLens</PageTitle>

<div class="tflens-stack" data-testid="misses-page">

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
        <div>
            <TypographyH2>Misses &amp; rework</TypographyH2>
            <TypographyMuted>@Subtitle</TypographyMuted>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="misses-period-label">@PeriodLabel</Badge>
            <div class="tflens-period">
                @* TR-020: SelectValue renders the raw bound value until SelectContent has rendered once,
                   so the closed trigger read "all" rather than "All history (default)". DisplayTextSelector
                   is the library's own hook and resolves it without waiting for the popover. *@
                <Select TValue="string"
                        Value="@objPeriod"
                        ValueChanged="OnPeriodChangedAsync"
                        DisplayTextSelector="@PeriodTextOf"
                        Class="w-full">
                    <SelectTrigger data-testid="misses-period">
                        <SelectValue Placeholder="All history (default)" />
                    </SelectTrigger>
                    <SelectContent>
                        @foreach (var vOption in PeriodOptions)
                        {
                            <SelectItem TValue="string" Value="@vOption.Key" Text="@vOption.Label">@vOption.Label</SelectItem>
                        }
                    </SelectContent>
                </Select>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (IsPlaybook)
    {
        <PlaybookAxisNote />
    }
    else
    {
        @* BRD-118 / REQ-NFR-013 clause 6 — two escape figures on this site, and they are not the same
           number. The note is standing page copy, never a tooltip. *@
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Info" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="miss-escape-note">
            <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>Two escape figures on this site, and they are not the same number</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>
                This page's <b>escape share</b> is <span class="font-mono">found_by &#8712; {owner, production}</span>
                &#247; all misses, from <span class="font-mono">misses.jsonl</span>. The <b>escape rate</b> on
                Gate outcomes keeps its own definition and its own source (<span class="font-mono">gates.jsonl</span>).
                They are adjacent, never merged.
            </AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
    }

    @if (!objIsLoaded)
    {
        <Card>
            <CardContent Class="p-6">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-full" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-3/4" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-1/2" />
                </div>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    }
    else if (objLoadError is not null)
    {
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Danger" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="misses-error">
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>Couldn't compute the miss view</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>@objLoadError</AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
    }
    else if (IsPlaybook)
    {
        @* REQ-UI-051 / BRD-167 — the Playbook axis renders real figures wherever the Playbook emits
           them, under the Playbook's OWN guards (PlaybookMissGuards), which are stricter than this
           page's and are never relaxed to match them. The surface owns its own empty state, because
           BRD-126's PlaybookEmpty is now a condition of the data rather than the permanent shape of the
           axis. The Framework switch is rendered, never hidden, either way. *@
        <PlaybookMissesSurface Misses="@objPeriodMisses"
                               Fixes="@objPeriodFixes"
                               Amends="@objPeriodAmends"
                               Runs="@objPeriodRuns" />
    }
    else if (objResult.MissesTotal == 0)
    {
        <Empty Title="No misses recorded yet"
               Description="TfLens reads docs/metrics/misses.jsonl; it never writes one. Connect a repo that emits the misses stream, or log a miss from the framework."
               Size="EmptySize.Default"
               data-testid="misses-empty">
            <Icon>
                <LucideIcon Name="bug" Size="40" />
            </Icon>
            <ChildContent>
                <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline" Href="/repos" data-testid="misses-empty-connect">
                    <LucideIcon Name="git-branch" Size="16" />
                    Manage repos
                </Button>
            </ChildContent>
        </Empty>
    }
    else
    {
        @* project_type is the only shape a miss figure is ever computed in (REQ-FN-077). There is
           deliberately no "all types" entry on MissAnalysis.Live, so the segment is chosen here and the
           bands below render exactly one of them. *@
        <Tabs Value="@objSelectedType" ValueChanged="OnTypeSelectedAsync" data-testid="miss-type">
            <TabsList>
                @foreach (var vType in objResult.ProjectTypes)
                {
                    @* TR-010: TabsTrigger captures no unmatched attributes, so the test id sits on its
                       own label span; a click on that still activates the trigger. *@
                    <TabsTrigger Value="@vType">
                        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5" data-testid="@($"miss-type-{vType}")">
                            <span>@vType</span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">@SegmentOf(vType).Misses</Badge>
                        </span>
                    </TabsTrigger>
                }
            </TabsList>
        </Tabs>

        var vSeg = SegmentOf(objSelectedType);
        var vTaint = SegmentTaint;

        @* ── BAND 1 — KPI row ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="tflens-stack" data-testid="miss-kpis">
            <div class="tflens-kpi-row tflens-kpi-4">
                <StatGroup Columns="4">
                    <StatTile Title="Open misses"
                              Value="@vSeg.OpenMisses.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
                              Description="@OpenDetail"
                              IconName="bug"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Destructive"
                              data-testid="kpi-open" />
                    <StatTile Title="Declined (wont-fix)"
                              Value="@vSeg.WontFix.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
                              Description="a decision, not a backlog item — never folded into open"
                              IconName="x"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart4"
                              data-testid="kpi-wontfix" />
                    <StatTile Title="@($"Misses {PeriodTileSuffix}")"
                              Value="@vSeg.Misses.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)"
                              Description="@MixDetail(vSeg)"
                              IconName="activity"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                              data-testid="kpi-period" />
                    <StatTile Title="Median time to close"
                              Description="miss-fix.ts − miss.ts over misses whose latest verdict is Verified"
                              IconName="clock"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart5"
                              data-testid="kpi-median-close">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@vSeg.MedianTimeToCloseHours"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(vSeg.MedianTimeToCloseHours)"
                                        TestId="kpi-median-close-value" />
                            @if (vSeg.MedianTimeToCloseHours.HasValue)
                            {
                                <span class="ml-1 text-base font-normal text-muted-foreground">h</span>
                            }
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                </StatGroup>
            </div>

            <div class="tflens-kpi-row tflens-kpi-4">
                <StatGroup Columns="4">
                    <StatTile Title="Design-miss share"
                              Description="@DesignShareDetail(vSeg)"
                              IconName="book-open"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart3"
                              data-testid="kpi-design-share">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@vSeg.DesignMissShare"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(vSeg.DesignMissShare)"
                                        TestId="kpi-design-share-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                    <StatTile Title="Escape share (misses)"
                              Description="@EscapeShareDetail(vSeg)"
                              IconName="triangle-alert"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart2"
                              data-testid="kpi-escape-share">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@vSeg.EscapeShare"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(vSeg.EscapeShare)"
                                        TestId="kpi-escape-share-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                    <StatTile Title="Tokens spent on rework"
                              Description="@SoleTokensDetail(vSeg)"
                              IconName="database"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                              data-testid="kpi-rework-tokens">
                        <ValueContent>
                            <FigureText Value="@vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.Sole"
                                        Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.Sole)"
                                        TestId="kpi-rework-tokens-value" />
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                    @* REQ-UI-036, restored 2026-08-29 — docs/mockups/misses.html rings this tile and puts
                       an `opencode · measured` badge on its face, because it is the ONLY measured dollar
                       figure in the product and the estimate card directly below carries a number an
                       order of magnitude larger. The mockup's own note is explicit that a reader who
                       cannot tell the two apart at a glance "has been given a plausible wrong number";
                       the build had dropped both the ring and the badge, which is precisely that reader.
                       The tile also carried a green tick where the mockup uses the database glyph — the
                       tick reads as a verdict on the figure rather than as its provenance. *@
                    <StatTile Title="Measured USD on rework"
                              Description="@MeasuredUsdDetail(vSeg)"
                              IconName="database"
                              Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                              Class="tflens-measured"
                              data-testid="kpi-rework-usd">
                        <TitleAdornment>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                                   Class="tflens-measured-badge"
                                   data-testid="kpi-rework-usd-measured-badge">opencode · measured</Badge>
                        </TitleAdornment>
                        <ValueContent>
                            <span data-testid="kpi-rework-usd-value">@MeasuredUsdDisplay(vSeg)</span>
                        </ValueContent>
                    </StatTile>
                </StatGroup>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* BRD-123 / REQ-NFR-013 clause 5 — rate-card dollars are never presented as spend. Its own card,
           its own row, a dashed border and the estimate label on its face. Nobody was billed this. *@
        <Card Class="tflens-estimate" data-testid="kpi-rework-usd-estimate">
            <CardContent Class="p-6">
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-4">
                    <span class="tflens-stat-chip tflens-accent-4 shrink-0">
                        <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
                    </span>
                    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
                            <span class="text-base font-semibold">@EstimateHarnessTitle rework —</span>
                            <span class="tflens-money-inline tabular-nums" data-testid="kpi-rework-usd-estimate-value">
                                @EstimateUsdDisplay
                            </span>
                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="kpi-rework-usd-estimate-label">
                                @RateCard.EstimateLabel
                            </Badge>
                        </div>
                        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                            A separate card on a separate row with a different treatment, deliberately: a reader
                            who cannot tell this apart from the measured tile at a glance has been given a
                            plausible wrong number. Exported under a key ending
                            <span class="font-mono">_usd_estimate</span>; the measured tile's key does not.
                            Priced from <span class="font-mono">@objRateCardPath</span>.
                            @EstimateBasis
                        </p>
                        @if (UnpricedModels.Count > 0)
                        {
                            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="kpi-rework-usd-unpriced">
                                Not priced by the rate card, so left out of the estimate rather than costed at zero:
                                <span class="font-mono">@string.Join(" · ", UnpricedModels)</span>.
                            </p>
                        }
                    </div>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>

        @* ── BAND 2 — where misses come from ──────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">Where misses come from</TypographyH2>
        <div class="tflens-grid tflens-grid-origin">

            <Card data-testid="miss-origin">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>Origin phase × miss class</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Did we specify badly, or build badly?</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">linked only</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (OriginRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-none">
                            No miss in this segment carries <span class="font-mono">origin_confidence: "linked"</span>,
                            so there is no per-origin figure to state. That is an absence of attribution, not a zero.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        @* A cross-tab: the columns are whichever miss_class values the linked records
                           actually carry, so this is a plain table rather than a DataTable — DataTableColumn
                           needs a compile-time property per column and miss_class has no closed vocabulary. *@
                        <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                            <table class="tflens-table tflens-table-origin" aria-label="Misses by origin phase and miss class">
                                <thead>
                                    <tr>
                                        <th>Origin phase</th>
                                        @foreach (var vClass in OriginClasses)
                                        {
                                            <th class="tflens-num">@vClass</th>
                                        }
                                        <th class="tflens-num">Total</th>
                                        <th class="tflens-num">Runs</th>
                                        <th class="tflens-num">Misses per run</th>
                                    </tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    @foreach (var vRow in OriginRows)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="@($"miss-origin-{vRow.Phase}")">
                                            <td><span class="font-mono">@vRow.Phase</span></td>
                                            @foreach (var vClass in OriginClasses)
                                            {
                                                <td class="tflens-num">@vRow.CountOf(vClass)</td>
                                            }
                                            <td class="tflens-num font-semibold">@vRow.Total</td>
                                            <td class="tflens-num">@(vRow.Runs is { } vRuns ? vRuns.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : Missing)</td>
                                            <td class="tflens-num">
                                                @if (vRow.Rate is { } vRate)
                                                {
                                                    <FigureText Value="@vRate" Class="text-xs" />
                                                }
                                                else
                                                {
                                                    @Missing
                                                }
                                            </td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                    @if (vTaint.AttributionExcluded > 0)
                                    {
                                        <tr data-testid="miss-origin-unattributed">
                                            <td class="text-muted-foreground">unattributed</td>
                                            @foreach (var vClass in OriginClasses)
                                            {
                                                <td class="tflens-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                            }
                                            <td class="tflens-num font-semibold">@vTaint.AttributionExcluded</td>
                                            <td class="tflens-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                            <td class="tflens-num text-muted-foreground">@Missing</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    }
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    @* BRD-121 — the exclusion is on the page, always, even at zero. An exclusion the reader
                       cannot see is indistinguishable from a bug. *@
                    <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-taint-count">
                        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="14" />
                        <span>
                            <b>@vTaint.AttributionExcluded of @vSeg.Misses misses excluded</b> from every per-origin
                            figure@(ExcludedBreakdown(vTaint)) — @vTaint.Reason.
                        </span>
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            <Card data-testid="miss-whymissed">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>Which practice failed</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>
                                Is our <b>specification</b> weak, or our <b>verification</b>?
                            </CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        @* BRD-119 — the denominator is on the card's face, never a tooltip. *@
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="miss-whymissed-denominator">
                            @AssessedLine(vSeg)
                        </Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                        <DataTable TData="PracticeRow"
                                   Data="@PracticeRows"
                                   ShowToolbar="false"
                                   ShowPagination="false"
                                   InitialPageSize="32"
                                   AriaLabel="Failed-practice distribution over misses that carry why_missed"
                                   data-testid="miss-whymissed-table">
                            <Columns>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PracticeRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Practice)" Header="why_missed">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Practice</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="PracticeRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Share)" Header="Share">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                            <Progress Value="@vRow.SharePercent" Class="w-16" />
                                            <span class="text-xs tabular-nums">@vRow.Count · @vRow.Share</span>
                                        </div>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                            </Columns>
                        </DataTable>
                    </div>
                    @if (vSeg.FailedPracticeNote is { } vNote)
                    {
                        <p class="mt-4 text-xs italic text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-whymissed-note">@vNote</p>
                    }
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-whymissed-eligibility">
                        @WhyMissedFooter(vSeg)
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ── BAND 2b — whose gap was it (REQ-UI-052, BRD-171, BRD-172) ────────────────── *@
        <Card data-testid="miss-sort">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                    <div>
                        <CardTitle>Whose gap was it</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            The card beside this one says <b>what broke</b>. This one says
                            <b>what to do about it</b> — and each answer has a different fixed remedy.
                        </CardDescription>
                    </div>
                    @* BRD-172 — `n of N sorted` on the card's face, never a tooltip, and never a
                       percentage of all misses. *@
                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="miss-sort-denominator">
                        @SortedLine(vSeg)
                    </Badge>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                    <DataTable TData="SortRow"
                               Data="@SortRows"
                               ShowToolbar="false"
                               ShowPagination="false"
                               InitialPageSize="16"
                               AriaLabel="Whose gap it was, over misses that carry the sort field"
                               data-testid="miss-sort-table">
                        <Columns>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="SortRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Answer)" Header="Whose gap">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="text-sm">@vRow.Answer</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="SortRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Share)" Header="@SortShareHeader(vSeg)">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                                        <Progress Value="@vRow.SharePercent" Class="w-16" />
                                        <span class="text-xs tabular-nums">@vRow.Count · @vRow.Share</span>
                                    </div>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="SortRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Response)" Header="The fixed response">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">@vRow.Response</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                        </Columns>
                    </DataTable>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                    @* BRD-172 — the records written before the field existed are stated APART, in those
                       words. A record from before the question was asked is not a record that declined
                       to answer it, and the two are never added together. *@
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-sort-predates">
                        @SortPredatesLine(vSeg)
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-sort-amended">
                        @SortAmendedLine()
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-sort-words">
                        Written in words, not raw values. The stream stores
                        <span class="font-mono">spec</span> · <span class="font-mono">unsaid</span> ·
                        <span class="font-mono">weak-check</span> · <span class="font-mono">ignored</span>;
                        nobody reading this page should have to know that.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>

        @* ── BAND 3 — who was running ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">Who was running</TypographyH2>

        @* BRD-124 — standing page copy, not a tooltip. *@
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="miss-observational">
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>Observational only — this band does not show causation</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>
                Miss counts per model and per agent are confounded by <i>which model gets the hard work</i>.
                Read these as a description of what ran, not as a ranking. Computed from
                <span class="font-mono">origin_confidence: "linked"</span> records only
                (@vTaint.AttributedN of @vSeg.Misses).
            </AlertDescription>
        </Alert>

        <div class="tflens-grid tflens-grid-2">
            <Card data-testid="miss-origin-model">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>By origin model</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Which model to route to — a different question from the one beside it</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@vTaint.AttributedN linked</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (ModelRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-model-none">
                            No <span class="font-mono">linked</span> miss names an origin model. The emitter forces
                            the model to <span class="font-mono">null</span> whenever its lookup fails, so this is
                            absence rather than a zero.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                            <DataTable TData="OriginCountRow"
                                       Data="@ModelRows"
                                       ShowToolbar="false"
                                       ShowPagination="false"
                                       InitialPageSize="32"
                                       AriaLabel="Misses by origin model, linked records only"
                                       data-testid="miss-origin-model-table">
                                <Columns>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Key)" Header="Model">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Key</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="int"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Count)" Header="Misses"
                                                     CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="tabular-nums">@vRow.Count</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Share)" Header="Share"
                                                     CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="tabular-nums text-xs">@vRow.Share</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                </Columns>
                            </DataTable>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            <Card data-testid="miss-origin-agent">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>By origin agent</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Which persona's instructions to tighten</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">@vTaint.AttributedN linked</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    @if (AgentRows.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-origin-agent-none">
                            No <span class="font-mono">linked</span> miss names an origin agent.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                            <DataTable TData="OriginCountRow"
                                       Data="@AgentRows"
                                       ShowToolbar="false"
                                       ShowPagination="false"
                                       InitialPageSize="32"
                                       AriaLabel="Misses by origin agent, linked records only"
                                       data-testid="miss-origin-agent-table">
                                <Columns>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Key)" Header="Agent">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Key</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="int"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Count)" Header="Misses"
                                                     CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="tabular-nums">@vRow.Count</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Share)" Header="Share"
                                                     CellClass="text-right">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="tabular-nums text-xs">@vRow.Share</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                    <DataTableColumn TData="OriginCountRow" TValue="string"
                                                     Property="@(aRow => aRow.Dominant)" Header="Dominant class">
                                        <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                            <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Dominant</span>
                                        </CellTemplate>
                                    </DataTableColumn>
                                </Columns>
                            </DataTable>
                        </div>
                    }
                </CardContent>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ── BAND 4 — cost of rework ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">Cost of rework</TypographyH2>
        <div class="tflens-grid tflens-grid-3" data-testid="miss-cost">

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="miss-cost-measured">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>Measured</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription><span class="font-mono">cost_attribution: sole</span></CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tflens-stat-chip tflens-accent-2 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="circle-check" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-money tabular-nums">
                        <FigureText Value="@vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.Sole"
                                    Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.Sole)"
                                    TestId="miss-cost-sole" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                        output tokens per miss fixed, over @vSeg.Cost.SoleRecords
                        @(vSeg.Cost.SoleRecords == 1 ? "fix" : "fixes") whose run touched exactly this REQ.
                        The whole window is this miss's cost — <b>this is a measurement</b>.
                    </p>
                    <Separator Class="mt-4 mb-4" />
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Measured USD (OpenCode)</span>
                        <span class="font-semibold tabular-nums" data-testid="miss-cost-measured-usd">@MeasuredUsdDisplay(vSeg)</span>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="miss-cost-apportioned">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>Apportioned</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription><span class="font-mono">cost_attribution: shared:n</span></CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tflens-stat-chip tflens-accent-4 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-money tabular-nums">
                        <FigureText Value="@vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.Apportioned"
                                    Class="@SmallWhenNoNumber(vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.Apportioned)"
                                    TestId="miss-cost-apportioned-value" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                        output tokens per miss, divided equally across @vSeg.Cost.SharedRecords
                        @(vSeg.Cost.SharedRecords == 1 ? "fix" : "fixes") that each repaired several misses.
                        One token window over several misses — <b>arithmetic, not measurement</b>, and never
                        summed into the column beside it.
                    </p>
                    <Separator Class="mt-4 mb-4" />
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Divided equally, and we say so</span>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">apportioned</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="miss-cost-unattributable">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div>
                            <CardTitle>Unattributable</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription><span class="font-mono">cost_attribution: none</span></CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tflens-stat-chip tflens-accent-danger shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="x" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-money tabular-nums" data-testid="miss-cost-none">
                        @vSeg.Cost.TokensPerMissFixed.NoneCount
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                        fixes with <b>no numbers at all</b> — the run's <span class="font-mono">tokens_scope</span>
                        was <span class="font-mono">none</span>, or the repair happened inline with no distinct fix
                        run (the <span class="font-mono">*log-miss --fixed</span> front door omits
                        <span class="font-mono">fix_run_id</span> deliberately). A count, never a divisor.
                    </p>
                    <Separator Class="mt-4 mb-4" />
                    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
                        <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">No <span class="font-mono">cost_attribution</span> at all</span>
                        <span class="font-semibold tabular-nums" data-testid="miss-cost-attribution-missing">@vSeg.Cost.AttributionMissing</span>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
            </Card>
        </div>

        <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-cost-no-blend">
            <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="14" />
            <span>
                There is no blended figure on this page, in the export or in parity —
                <span class="font-mono">MissCost</span> exposes <span class="font-mono">Sole</span>,
                <span class="font-mono">Apportioned</span> and <span class="font-mono">NoneCount</span> and nothing
                else, so a single combined number has no property to bind to (ADR-019).
            </span>
        </p>

        @* ── BAND 5 — what reviews cost (REQ-UI-054, BRD-175) ─────────────────────────── *@
        <TypographyH2 Class="text-lg">What reviews cost</TypographyH2>

        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Default" data-testid="miss-review-note">
            <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>The only record anywhere that prices a specification defect</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>
                A dashboard that shows what building and verifying cost, but not what reviewing cost, tells
                its reader that documents are free. Every figure below is <b>copied from the record</b> — the
                emitter copied it from the two runs the record names. TfLens computes none of them, and where
                a figure is absent it says <span class="font-mono">not available</span> rather than showing a
                zero. A <span class="font-mono">review</span> record is <b>not a miss</b>: none of these rows
                appears in any count, chart or filter elsewhere on this page.
            </AlertDescription>
        </Alert>

        <Card data-testid="miss-review-cost">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                    <div>
                        <CardTitle>Owner review, per phase</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            Corrections given, what the reviewed output cost to produce, and what applying the
                            corrections cost
                        </CardDescription>
                    </div>
                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">copied · never computed</Badge>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                @if (ReviewRows.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-review-none">
                        No <span class="font-mono">review</span> record has arrived on this segment's miss
                        stream yet, so there is nothing to price. That is an absence of records, not a review
                        that cost nothing.
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    @* A plain table for the same reason the origin cross-tab is one: every cell here is a
                       copied figure that must be able to read `not available`, and the row's own phase is
                       the key rather than a sortable value. *@
                    <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                        <table class="tflens-table" aria-label="What each owner review cost, copied from the record">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Review phase</th>
                                    <th class="tflens-num">Corrections</th>
                                    <th class="tflens-num">Cost to produce</th>
                                    <th class="tflens-num">Cost to correct</th>
                                    <th class="tflens-num">Correction as share</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                @foreach (var vRow in ReviewRows)
                                {
                                    <tr data-testid="@($"miss-review-{vRow.Phase}")">
                                        <td><span class="font-mono text-xs tflens-review-phase">@vRow.Phase</span></td>
                                        <td class="tflens-num">
                                            @if (vRow.Corrections is { } vCorrections)
                                            {
                                                <span class="tabular-nums">@vCorrections.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</span>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <span class="text-xs italic text-muted-foreground">@NotAvailable</span>
                                            }
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="tflens-num">
                                            @RenderReviewCost(vRow.TokensProduce, vRow.CostProduceUsd)
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="tflens-num">
                                            @RenderReviewCost(vRow.TokensCorrect, vRow.CostCorrectUsd)
                                        </td>
                                        <td class="tflens-num">
                                            <span class="text-xs @(vRow.CorrectionShare is null ? "text-muted-foreground" : "tabular-nums")">
                                                @(vRow.CorrectionShare ?? Missing)
                                            </span>
                                        </td>
                                    </tr>
                                }
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                }
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
                    <p class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-review-notavailable">
                        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="14" />
                        <span>
                            <b><span class="font-mono">@NotAvailable</span>, never <span class="font-mono">0</span>.</b>
                            A review whose record names its two runs but whose token windows the emitter could
                            not copy carries no figure at all, and a zero there would read as a review that
                            cost nothing. <i>Correction as share</i> is the ratio of the two copied figures and
                            is left blank unless both are present — it is not a third cost, and nothing on this
                            row is re-derived, apportioned or summed.
                        </span>
                    </p>
                    <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-review-phases">
                        @ReviewPhasesLine()
                    </p>
                </div>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>

        @* ── Per-miss detail ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <Card data-testid="miss-detail">
            <CardHeader>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
                    <div>
                        <CardTitle>Every miss</CardTitle>
                        <CardDescription>
                            @DetailRows.Count @(DetailRows.Count == 1 ? "record" : "records") · each row carries the
                            one sentence that was written about it · the toolbar filter searches REQ, class and
                            whose gap · amendments folded at read time, so a
                            <span class="font-mono">why_missed</span> or a <span class="font-mono">sort</span>
                            supplied later shows here
                        </CardDescription>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                <div class="tflens-scroll-x">
                    @* TR-009: InitialPageSize is set explicitly — the grid truncates to it even when
                       pagination is off, so it is never left at the default 5. *@
                    <DataTable TData="MissRow"
                               Data="@DetailRows"
                               ShowToolbar="true"
                               ShowPagination="true"
                               InitialPageSize="25"
                               AriaLabel="Every miss in this segment"
                               data-testid="miss-detail-table">
                        <Columns>
                            @* REQ-UI-053 / BRD-173 — the record's own one-sentence `what`, in the owner's
                               words, on the row itself. A miss identified only by a class and a date is
                               unrecognisable a month later. *@
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.MissId)" Header="Miss — what happened">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <div class="tflens-miss-cell">
                                        <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Link"
                                                Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                                OnClick="@(() => ShowRaw(vRow.MissId))"
                                                data-testid="@($"miss-raw-{vRow.MissId}")">
                                            <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.MissId</span>
                                        </Button>
                                        <div class="text-xs text-muted-foreground @(vRow.HasWhat ? string.Empty : "italic")"
                                             data-testid="miss-what">@vRow.What</div>
                                    </div>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.ReqId)" Header="REQ" Filterable="true">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.ReqId</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.MissClass)" Header="Class" Filterable="true">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"><span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.MissClass</span></Badge>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            @* REQ-UI-052 / BRD-171 — the filter on `sort` the band above names. The column
                               carries the WORDS, so the toolbar search matches what the reader can see; the
                               raw value never reaches this page. *@
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.WhoseGap)" Header="Whose gap" Filterable="true">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tflens-gap-cell text-xs @(vRow.HasSort ? string.Empty : "italic text-muted-foreground")">@vRow.WhoseGap</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Severity)" Header="Severity">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <Badge Variant="@vRow.SeverityVariant">@vRow.Severity</Badge>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Origin)" Header="Origin">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1">
                                        <span class="font-mono text-xs">@vRow.Origin</span>
                                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">@vRow.Confidence</Badge>
                                    </span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.FoundBy)" Header="Found by">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="text-xs">@vRow.FoundBy</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Status)" Header="Status">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <Badge Variant="@vRow.StatusVariant">@vRow.Status</Badge>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="MissRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Tokens)" Header="Tokens"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-1">
                                        <span class="tabular-nums text-xs">@vRow.Tokens</span>
                                        @if (vRow.Attribution is { Length: > 0 })
                                        {
                                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">@vRow.Attribution</Badge>
                                        }
                                    </span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                        </Columns>
                    </DataTable>
                </div>

                @* BRD-173 / BRD-84 — the ONE prose field that travels from a stream onto a TfLens
                   surface, said on the page so a reader can check it. Requirement text from a checklist
                   is never stored, rendered or exported, and this clause does not relax that. *@
                <p class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-what-note">
                    <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="14" />
                    <span>
                        The sentence on each row is the record's own <span class="font-mono">what</span> field,
                        in the owner's words. It is the <b>only prose that travels</b> from a stream onto this
                        page — requirement text from a checklist is never stored, rendered or exported.
                        @WhatEligibilityLine(vSeg)
                    </span>
                </p>

                <div class="mt-4">
                    <Collapsible @bind-Open="objIsRawOpen">
                        <Card>
                            <CardContent Class="p-4">
                                <CollapsibleTrigger>
                                    <span class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium" data-testid="miss-raw-trigger">
                                        <LucideIcon Name="@(objIsRawOpen ? "chevron-down" : "chevron-right")" Size="16" />
                                        Raw record — <span class="font-mono">@RawMissId</span>
                                    </span>
                                </CollapsibleTrigger>
                                <CollapsibleContent>
                                    @* TR-018: a closed CollapsibleContent still lays its children out and overlaps
                                       what follows, so the subtree is guarded here rather than merely hidden. *@
                                    @if (objIsRawOpen)
                                    {
                                        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-2">
                                            <CodeBlock Title="@($"miss · {RawMissId}")" Code="@RawJson" data-testid="miss-raw" />
                                            <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="miss-raw-note">
                                                Field <i>names</i> only for <span class="font-mono">overflow</span> — SCHEMA.md §9
                                                keeps undocumented payloads off every screen. A
                                                <span class="font-mono">why_missed</span>, a
                                                <span class="font-mono">sort</span> or a
                                                <span class="font-mono">what</span> shown here may have arrived on a later
                                                <span class="font-mono">miss-amend</span> and been folded in at read time; the
                                                stored <span class="font-mono">miss</span> row still carries
                                                <span class="font-mono">null</span>, because an amend completes a record and
                                                never edits it.
                                            </p>
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </CollapsibleContent>
                            </CardContent>
                        </Card>
                    </Collapsible>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What an absent string or an absent cost renders as — never a blank, never <c>$0.00</c>.</summary>
    private const string Missing = "—";

    /// <summary>
    /// What an absent <b>review</b> figure reads as (BRD-175).
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// A review's costs are the one place an em dash is not enough: the record names two runs, so a blank
    /// invites the reader to assume the run cost nothing. It says so in words instead, and never <c>0</c>.
    /// </remarks>
    private const string NotAvailable = "not available";

    /// <summary>
    /// The English each <c>sort</c> value is rendered as, and the fixed remedy it names (BRD-171).
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// One spelling in one place: the band, the per-miss row and the filter all read this table, so the
    /// raw token — <c>weak-check</c> — never reaches the page. The keys are
    /// <see cref="MissAmendFolder.AmendableFields"/>'s closed vocabulary for <c>sort</c>, which is the same
    /// list the producer writes and an amend is validated against; a value outside it is surfaced as it
    /// stands rather than coerced to the nearest of the four (BRD-170).
    /// </remarks>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyDictionary<string, SortWording> SortVocabulary =
        new Dictionary<string, SortWording>(StringComparer.Ordinal)
        {
            [MissSorts.WeakCheck] = new(
                "There was a check and it did not catch it",
                "Fix the check, not the prose"),
            [MissSorts.Unsaid] = new(
                "The framework never said it anywhere",
                "Add one requirement line, plus a check"),
            [MissSorts.Ignored] = new(
                "It was written down and ignored anyway",
                "Make it a hook or a script, or delete the rule"),
            [MissSorts.Spec] = new(
                "The project's own specification did not say it",
                "Fix the checklist line; the framework is untouched")
        };

    /// <summary>The period key that means the whole history, and the page's default (BRD-125).</summary>
    private const string AllHistory = "all";

    /// <summary>The one harness whose dollars are measured rather than estimated (SCHEMA.md §4).</summary>
    private const string OpenCodeHarness = "opencode";

    /// <summary>The <c>tokens_scope</c> that excludes a fix record from every cost figure.</summary>
    private const string NoTokenScope = "none";

    /// <summary>The period choices, all history first because it is the default.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<PeriodOption> PeriodOptions =
    [
        new PeriodOption(AllHistory, "All history (default)", null, "all history"),
        new PeriodOption("7", "Last 7 days", 7, "last 7 days"),
        new PeriodOption("30", "Last 30 days", 30, "last 30 days"),
        new PeriodOption("90", "Last 90 days", 90, "last 90 days")
    ];

    private IReadOnlyList<MissRecord> objAllMisses = [];
    private IReadOnlyList<MissFixRecord> objAllFixes = [];
    private IReadOnlyList<MissAmendRecord> objAllAmends = [];
    private IReadOnlyList<RunRecord> objAllRuns = [];

    private IReadOnlyList<MissReviewRecord> objAllReviews = [];

    private IReadOnlyList<MissFixRecord> objPeriodFixes = [];

    // REQ-UI-054 / BRD-174 — reviews are a FOURTH kind and never a miss. They are kept in their own
    // list, they are never folded, never counted and never handed to MissFigures.Compute; the only
    // control that reads them is the review band.
    private IReadOnlyList<MissReviewRecord> objPeriodReviews = [];

    // The window's raw records, kept beside the folded ones because the Playbook surface folds and
